{#
    Overall, or one season. The site's shared scope selector.

    <twig:ScopeSwitch route="records_board" :seasons="seasons"
                      :activeSlug="current_season ? current_season.slug : null" />

    Links rather than a control, and for the same reason the import screen's
    preview is a form submit: the scope belongs in the URL. Every scope is then
    reachable, linkable and back-buttonable, and switching needs no script —
    which the one script this site ships is not allowed to become.

    `route` is the page being scoped, so the same selector serves the records
    board, the tournament archive and anything else that reads `?season=`.
    `routeParams` carries whatever else that route needs in its path — the
    player profile's own slug, which is not a scope and does not change when
    the scope does.

    The leaderboard has no `ScopeSwitch` at all, deliberately. Option 5C: it is
    the points view and points are season-specific, so it can offer no Overall
    without manufacturing one. It carries a plain link to `/seasons` instead.
#}
{% props route, seasons = [], activeSlug = null, overall = 'Overall', routeParams = {} %}

{% set scopes = [{label: overall, slug: null}] %}
{% for season in seasons %}
    {% set scopes = scopes|merge([{label: season.name, slug: season.slug}]) %}
{% endfor %}

<nav {{ attributes.defaults({class: 'flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2'}) }} aria-label="Season scope">
    {% for scope in scopes %}
        {% set active = scope.slug == activeSlug %}
        <a href="{{ scope.slug ? path(route, routeParams|merge({'season': scope.slug})) : path(route, routeParams) }}"
           {% if active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
           class="rounded-control border px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold transition-colors outline-none {{ active
               ? 'border-brand-strong bg-brand-strong/10 text-brand'
               : 'border-line bg-surface text-ink-muted hover:border-line hover:text-ink focus:text-ink' }}">{{ scope.label }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
</nav>
